<Base
  title="Our Promises | TheCalcUniverse"
  description="The rules this site will never break: no popups, no ad ambushes, pages under 300KB, and calculators that are never covered by anything."
>
  <article class="article">
    <h1>Our promises</h1>
    <p>These are not aspirations. They are rules, and breaking any of them is a bug.</p>
    <div class="faq-item"><h3>1. The calculator is always above the fold — and nothing ever covers it.</h3>
      <p>No banner, no overlay, no “before you continue.” You came for an answer; it is on your screen immediately.</p></div>
    <div class="faq-item"><h3>2. No popups. Ever.</h3>
      <p>No newsletter modals, no notification prompts, no interstitials. If we ever run ads, they will sit in fixed, clearly separated spaces — never between you and your result.</p></div>
    <div class="faq-item"><h3>3. Pages stay under 300KB.</h3>
      <p>No web fonts, no third-party scripts on calculator pages, no megabytes of tracking. Fast is a feature you can measure.</p></div>
    <div class="faq-item"><h3>4. Your numbers never leave your device.</h3>
      <p>Every calculation runs in your browser. We do not transmit, store, or sell what you type.</p></div>
    <div class="faq-item"><h3>5. Every answer can be checked.</h3>
      <p>Formulas are shown on the page, worked with your numbers. Our engines are covered by automated tests against published examples from primary sources — see the <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a>.</p></div>
  </article>
</Base>
